# Mega Sale Migration — Implementation Plan (v2)

Migrate the Mega Sale feature from `permission_config`-based string storage to dedicated tables with SKU-level management, move admin UI from the Permissions page to a new "Mega Sale" tab in the Discount Rules page, implement server-side filtering with pagination, and fix broken storefront filters.

---

## Design Decisions (User-Confirmed)

1. **SKU-level granularity** — Each mega sale entry references a `product_sku_id` (variation). Admin can highlight specific color/size variations, not just whole products.
2. **No product limit** — Remove the hard-coded limit. Shop panel will use **cursor-based pagination** (infinite scroll) for the mega sale page.
3. **Server-side filtering** — The new API will return only mega sale products directly, with support for sort, search, stock filters, and pagination. This replaces the broken client-side filtering.

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database Schema (V2-036)

#### [NEW] `mega_sale_settings` table (single-row global config)

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `id` | TINYINT UNSIGNED (=1) | Singleton row |
| `is_active` | TINYINT(1) | Master on/off toggle |
| `campaign_end_at` | DATETIME NULL | Global campaign countdown |
| `default_end_at` | DATETIME NULL | Fallback per-product countdown |
| `updated_by_admin` | INT NULL | FK → admins |
| `created_at` / `updated_at` | TIMESTAMP | Audit timestamps |

#### [NEW] `mega_sale_products` table (per-SKU entries)

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `id` | BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INC | PK |
| `product_sku_id` | INT NOT NULL | FK → product_skus (variation) |
| `is_active` | TINYINT(1) | Per-SKU toggle |
| `end_at` | DATETIME NULL | Per-SKU timer (NULL = inherit global) |
| `serial` | INT | Display order |
| `created_at` / `updated_at` | TIMESTAMP | Audit timestamps |

#### Data migration
- Read existing `permission_config` `storefront_visibility.*` rows.
- Populate `mega_sale_settings` with global values.
- Parse `megasale_product_ids` + `megasale_product_timers` → insert into `mega_sale_products` (matching product IDs to their first SKU).
- Delete `storefront_visibility` rows from `permission_config`.

